EPIC-260715-2mqgvm_viability-and-foundation/STORY-260715-lkshfz_ssh-engine-spike/TASK-260728-yx2fca_rescope-ssh-transport-contract-to-m0-viability/README.md:7:In scope: revising the TASK-260715-2ny6z4 contract document and the TASK-260720-100wu6 candidate-neutral seam types/protocols; splitting requirements into M0-viability-mandatory and M3-deferred tiers; recording the exact deferred semantics (consumer-driven receive-window credit with immutable cap, RFC channel-open rejection reason taxonomy, exact exec-exit status/coreDumped metadata, deep rekey and keepalive observability) with their M3 owner task; updating consumer mapping for TASK-260715-1ozsb6, TASK-260715-2d3g5e, and TASK-260715-1u2vpc; updating precondition resources on affected tasks. Out of scope: weakening pre-auth host-key verification, approved authentication, direct-tcpip, exec/stdin upload, client-rekey trigger, bounded buffers, cancellation, lifecycle, Keychain-only secrets, or privacy-safe errors; adapter or engine implementation; NIOSSH fork work.
